
-- Add pms_policy_content column to app_settings
ALTER TABLE public.app_settings ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS pms_policy_content text;

-- Seed with the full PMS Policy document
UPDATE public.app_settings
SET pms_policy_content = E'# PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (PMS) POLICY\n\n## Document Control Information\n\n| Field | Details |\n|---|---|\n| Policy Name | Performance Management System (PMS) Policy |\n| Policy Number | HR-PMS-001 |\n| Version | 1.0 |\n| Effective Date | [To be determined] |\n| Review Date | [Annual review recommended] |\n| Policy Owner | Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO) |\n| Approved By | Board of Directors / Management Committee |\n| Distribution | All Employees, Managers, HR Team |\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. Executive Summary\n2. Policy Statement\n3. Scope and Applicability\n4. Definitions\n5. Roles and Responsibilities\n6. Performance Review Process\n7. Key Performance Indicators (KPI) Framework\n8. Rating Scale and Scoring Methodology\n9. Review Cycles and Timelines\n10. Multi-Level Approval Workflow\n11. Query and Observation System\n12. Performance Improvement Plans (PIP)\n13. Training Needs Identification (TNI)\n14. Appeals and Grievance Procedures\n15. Data Privacy and Security\n16. Compliance and Legal Requirements\n17. Policy Governance and Amendments\n18. Appendices\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n### 1.1 Purpose\n\nThis Performance Management System (PMS) Policy establishes a comprehensive framework for evaluating, developing, and recognizing employee performance across the organization. The policy aims to:\n\n- Align individual performance with organizational goals\n- Provide transparent and fair performance evaluation\n- Identify training and development needs\n- Support career progression and succession planning\n- Foster a culture of continuous improvement and accountability\n\n### 1.2 Key Principles\n\nThe PMS is built on the following core principles:\n\n- **Transparency**: All employees have clear visibility into performance expectations and evaluation criteria\n- **Fairness**: Consistent application of standards across all levels and departments\n- **Objectivity**: Data-driven assessments based on measurable KPIs\n- **Continuous Feedback**: Regular communication between employees and managers\n- **Development Focus**: Performance reviews as opportunities for growth, not just evaluation\n- **Accountability**: Clear ownership at every stage of the review process\n\n## 2. Policy Statement\n\n### 2.1 Organizational Commitment\n\nThe organization is committed to maintaining a performance management system that:\n\n- Recognizes and rewards high performance\n- Provides constructive feedback for improvement\n- Ensures compliance with applicable labor laws and regulations\n- Protects employee data privacy and confidentiality\n- Promotes equal opportunity and non-discrimination\n\n### 2.2 Management Responsibilities\n\nManagement at all levels is responsible for:\n\n- Setting clear, achievable performance expectations\n- Providing timely and constructive feedback\n- Supporting employee development\n- Conducting fair and unbiased evaluations\n- Maintaining confidentiality of performance data\n\n### 2.3 Employee Rights\n\nAll employees have the right to:\n\n- Understand their performance expectations and KPIs\n- Receive regular feedback on their performance\n- Access their performance records\n- Appeal performance ratings through established procedures\n- Request clarification or raise concerns about their evaluation\n\n## 3. Scope and Applicability\n\n### 3.1 Coverage\n\nThis policy applies to:\n\n- All permanent employees across all divisions, business units, and departments\n- Contractual employees on assignments exceeding 6 months (subject to contract terms)\n- Probationary employees (with modified review cycles)\n\n### 3.2 Exclusions\n\nThis policy does NOT apply to:\n\n- Temporary workers on assignments less than 6 months\n- Interns and trainees (covered under separate internship policies)\n- Board members and non-executive directors\n- External consultants and vendors\n\n### 3.3 Organizational Levels\n\nThe PMS covers employees at all levels:\n\n- **Executive Level**: C-suite and senior leadership\n- **Management Level**: Department heads, managers, team leads\n- **Professional Level**: Specialists, analysts, coordinators\n- **Operational Level**: Frontline staff, support roles\n\n## 4. Definitions\n\n### 4.1 Key Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| KPI (Key Performance Indicator) | A measurable value that demonstrates how effectively an employee is achieving key objectives |\n| KRA (Key Result Area) | A category or domain of responsibility within which KPIs are defined |\n| Review Period | The time frame for which performance is evaluated (e.g., Monthly, Quarterly, Annual) |\n| Self-Review | Employee''s self-assessment of their own performance against assigned KPIs |\n| Manager Review | Direct manager''s evaluation of employee performance |\n| Reporting Manager (RM) | The immediate supervisor responsible for an employee''s performance evaluation |\n| Skip-Level Manager | The manager one level above the direct reporting manager (RM2) |\n| HR PMS Team | Human Resources personnel responsible for validating and processing performance reviews |\n| Auditor | Independent reviewer who validates the accuracy and fairness of performance assessments |\n| Weightage | The relative importance of a KPI, expressed as a percentage of total performance |\n| Rating | Numerical score assigned to performance (0-5 scale) |\n| Threshold | Performance benchmarks (R0-R5) that determine rating levels |\n| Query | A formal question or clarification request raised during the review process |\n| Observation | Feedback or comment provided by a reviewer on employee performance |\n| PIP (Performance Improvement Plan) | A structured plan to help underperforming employees improve |\n| TNI (Training Needs Identification) | Process of identifying skill gaps requiring training intervention |\n\n### 4.2 Workflow Stages\n\n| Stage | Description |\n|---|---|\n| KRA Set | KPIs have been assigned to the employee |\n| Self Review | Employee has submitted their self-assessment |\n| Manager L1 Check | Direct manager (RM1) review in progress |\n| Manager L2 Check | Skip-level manager (RM2) review in progress |\n| HR PMS Review | HR team validation in progress |\n| Audit | Independent audit review in progress |\n| Management Review | Senior management final review in progress |\n| Approved | Performance review completed and approved |\n\n## 5. Roles and Responsibilities\n\n### 5.1 Employee Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Understand assigned KPIs and performance expectations\n- Submit self-reviews within specified timelines\n- Provide accurate data and evidence for achieved performance\n- Respond to queries and clarifications promptly\n- Participate constructively in performance discussions\n- Implement feedback and development recommendations\n\n**Timelines:**\n\n- Self-review submission: Within 7 days of review period end\n- Query response: Within 3 business days of query receipt\n- Evidence upload: At the time of self-review submission\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- Employees are accountable for the accuracy of self-reported performance data\n- Falsification of performance data may result in disciplinary action\n\n### 5.2 Reporting Manager Level 1 (RM1) Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Set clear, measurable KPIs aligned with organizational goals\n- Provide ongoing feedback and coaching throughout the review period\n- Conduct fair and objective performance evaluations\n- Review employee self-assessments and validate achieved values\n- Raise queries for clarification when needed\n- Approve or send back reviews with constructive feedback\n- Identify training needs and development opportunities\n\n**Timelines:**\n\n- KPI assignment: Within 5 days of review period start\n- Manager review completion: Within 3 business days of employee submission\n- Query resolution: Within 2 business days of employee response\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- RM1 is accountable for the quality and timeliness of performance reviews for direct reports\n- Failure to complete reviews within SLA may impact RM1''s own performance rating\n\n**Special Provisions:**\n\n- **Daily Binary KPI Override**: For daily binary KPIs (Yes/No), RM1 can override individual daily entries with mandatory justification\n- **Delegation**: RM1 can delegate review authority to a backup manager during planned absences (minimum 3 days advance notice required)\n\n### 5.3 Reporting Manager Level 2 (RM2) Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Review and validate RM1''s assessments for consistency and fairness\n- Provide skip-level oversight and calibration\n- Ensure alignment with departmental and organizational standards\n- Approve, query, or send back reviews to RM1 with rationale\n- Identify patterns and trends across teams\n- Escalate concerns about rating inflation or deflation\n\n**Timelines:**\n\n- RM2 review completion: Within 3 business days of RM1 approval\n- Calibration meetings: Quarterly (recommended)\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- RM2 is accountable for ensuring consistency in performance ratings across teams\n- RM2 has override authority over RM1 ratings with documented justification\n\n**Applicability:**\n\n- RM2 review is mandatory for:\n  - Employees at management level and above\n  - Employees with performance ratings below 3.0 (underperformers)\n  - Employees flagged for PIP or TNI\n- RM2 review is optional for:\n  - High performers (rating >= 4.5) - may be fast-tracked\n  - Junior-level employees (subject to departmental policy)\n\n### 5.4 HR PMS Team Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Validate completeness and compliance of all performance reviews\n- Ensure adherence to rating guidelines and organizational standards\n- Check for evidence submission and documentation quality\n- Identify anomalies, outliers, and potential bias\n- Coordinate with managers to resolve discrepancies\n- Generate performance analytics and reports for management\n- Maintain performance data integrity and confidentiality\n- Support employees and managers with PMS-related queries\n\n**Timelines:**\n\n- HR validation: Within 2 business days of RM2 approval\n- Bulk processing: For high-volume periods, up to 5 business days\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- HR PMS Team is the gatekeeper for performance data quality\n- HR has the authority to send reviews back to any previous stage if non-compliant\n\n**Validation Checklist:**\n\n- All mandatory fields completed\n- Evidence uploaded for KPIs requiring documentation\n- Ratings within acceptable range (no outliers without justification)\n- Remarks provided for low ratings (<3.0) and high ratings (>=4.5)\n- No pending queries or observations\n- Approval chain followed correctly\n\n### 5.5 Auditor Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Conduct independent audits of performance reviews for compliance\n- Validate accuracy of calculations and scoring\n- Ensure fairness and absence of bias\n- Review evidence and documentation quality\n- Flag irregularities for investigation\n- Provide audit reports to management\n\n**Timelines:**\n\n- Audit review: Within 2 business days of HR approval\n- Audit reports: Monthly summary to management\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- Auditors are accountable for the integrity and compliance of the PMS\n- Auditors report directly to senior management or compliance committee\n\n**Audit Scope:**\n\n- Mandatory Audit: All reviews with ratings <2.5 or >=4.8\n- Sample Audit: Random 10% sample of all other reviews\n- Triggered Audit: Reviews flagged by HR or management for investigation\n\n### 5.6 Management (Senior Leadership) Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Final approval of performance reviews (for designated employee levels)\n- Strategic oversight of organizational performance trends\n- Review and approve PIP recommendations\n- Ensure alignment of performance outcomes with business objectives\n- Make final decisions on appeals and grievances\n- Approve policy amendments and exceptions\n\n**Timelines:**\n\n- Management review: Within 2 business days of auditor approval\n- Appeals resolution: Within 10 business days of appeal submission\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- Management is accountable for the strategic effectiveness of the PMS\n- Management decisions on appeals are final\n\n**Applicability:**\n\n- Management review is mandatory for:\n  - Employees at senior management level (Grade 8 and above)\n  - All PIP cases\n  - Appeals and grievances\n- Management review is optional for:\n  - Other employee levels (delegated to HR PMS Team)\n\n### 5.7 System Administrator Responsibilities\n\n**Primary Duties:**\n\n- Configure and maintain the PMS application\n- Manage user access and permissions\n- Set up review periods, workflows, and approval chains\n- Generate system reports and analytics\n- Ensure data backup and disaster recovery\n- Provide technical support to users\n\n**Accountability:**\n\n- System Administrators are accountable for system uptime, data security, and user support\n\n## 6. Performance Review Process\n\n### 6.1 Process Overview\n\nThe performance review process consists of 8 sequential stages:\n\n```\n1. KRA Set -> 2. Self Review -> 3. Manager L1 Check -> 4. Manager L2 Check ->\n5. HR PMS Review -> 6. Audit -> 7. Management Review -> 8. Approved\n```\n\n### 6.2 Stage-by-Stage Process\n\n**Stage 1: KRA Set (KPI Assignment)**\n\n- **Who**: RM1 (with employee consultation)\n- **When**: Within 5 days of review period start\n- **What**:\n  - RM1 assigns KPIs to employees based on role, department goals, and organizational objectives\n  - KPIs include target values, weightage, UOM (Unit of Measurement), and rating thresholds (R0-R5)\n  - Employee reviews and acknowledges assigned KPIs\n  - Employee can request clarification or propose modifications (subject to RM1 approval)\n- **Deliverables**: Signed KPI assignment document (digital acknowledgment in PMS)\n\n**Stage 2: Self Review (Employee Submission)**\n\n- **Who**: Employee\n- **When**: Within 7 days of review period end\n- **What**:\n  - Employee enters achieved values for each KPI\n  - System auto-calculates ratings based on thresholds\n  - Employee provides remarks explaining performance (mandatory for ratings <3.0 or >=4.5)\n  - Employee uploads evidence documents (mandatory for KPIs marked as \"Require Evidence\")\n  - Employee submits self-review for manager approval\n- **Deliverables**: Completed self-review with achieved values, ratings, remarks, and evidence\n- **Special Cases**:\n  - Daily/Weekly KPIs: Employee submits daily/weekly entries throughout the period, then submits aggregated monthly review\n  - N/A KPIs: Employee can mark KPIs as \"Not Applicable\" with mandatory justification (minimum 50 characters)\n\n**Stage 3: Manager L1 Check (Direct Manager Review)**\n\n- **Who**: RM1\n- **When**: Within 3 business days of employee submission\n- **What**:\n  - RM1 reviews employee''s self-assessment and evidence\n  - RM1 validates achieved values and may adjust if discrepancies found\n  - RM1 provides manager rating and remarks\n  - RM1 can:\n    - **Approve**: Move to next stage (RM2 or HR, depending on workflow)\n    - **Raise Query**: Request clarification from employee\n    - **Send Back**: Return to employee for revision with reason\n    - **Override (Daily Binary KPIs)**: Adjust individual daily entries with justification\n- **Deliverables**: Manager rating, remarks, and approval decision\n- **Escalation**: If RM1 does not complete review within SLA, auto-escalate to RM2 after 5 business days\n\n**Stage 4: Manager L2 Check (Skip-Level Manager Review)**\n\n- **Who**: RM2\n- **When**: Within 3 business days of RM1 approval\n- **What**:\n  - RM2 reviews both employee and RM1 assessments\n  - RM2 ensures consistency and fairness across teams\n  - RM2 can:\n    - **Approve**: Move to HR PMS review\n    - **Send Back to RM1**: Request RM1 to reconsider with feedback\n    - **Send Back to Employee**: Request employee to revise (rare)\n    - **Override RM1 Rating**: Adjust rating with mandatory justification\n- **Deliverables**: RM2 validation, remarks, and approval decision\n- **Calibration**: RM2 conducts quarterly calibration sessions with RM1s to ensure rating consistency\n\n**Stage 5: HR PMS Review (HR Validation)**\n\n- **Who**: HR PMS Team\n- **When**: Within 2 business days of RM2 approval (or RM1 if RM2 skipped)\n- **What**:\n  - HR validates completeness, compliance, and data quality\n  - HR checks for rating anomalies and bias indicators\n  - HR ensures evidence is uploaded and adequate\n  - HR can:\n    - **Approve**: Move to Audit (if applicable) or Management Review\n    - **Send Back to RM1/RM2**: Request corrections or additional information\n    - **Flag for Investigation**: Escalate to management for potential policy violations\n- **Deliverables**: HR validation certificate (digital stamp in PMS)\n- **Bulk Processing**: HR can bulk-approve reviews that pass all validation checks\n\n**Stage 6: Audit (Independent Compliance Check)**\n\n- **Who**: Auditor\n- **When**: Within 2 business days of HR approval\n- **What**:\n  - Auditor conducts independent compliance audit\n  - Auditor validates calculations, evidence, and process adherence\n  - Auditor checks for fairness and absence of discrimination\n  - Auditor can:\n    - **Approve**: Move to Management Review\n    - **Send Back**: Return to any previous stage with audit findings\n    - **Escalate**: Flag serious compliance issues to management\n- **Deliverables**: Audit report with findings and recommendations\n- **Audit Scope**: Mandatory for all reviews with ratings <2.5 or >=4.8; Random 10% sample of all other reviews\n\n**Stage 7: Management Review (Final Approval)**\n\n- **Who**: Senior Management\n- **When**: Within 2 business days of Audit approval\n- **What**:\n  - Management conducts final review (for applicable employee levels)\n  - Management ensures alignment with organizational strategy\n  - Management approves PIP recommendations\n  - Management can:\n    - **Approve**: Finalize review (move to Approved stage)\n    - **Send Back**: Request revisions with strategic feedback\n- **Deliverables**: Management approval and final sign-off\n- **Applicability**: Mandatory for senior management level employees and PIP cases\n\n**Stage 8: Approved (Review Completed)**\n\n- **Who**: System (auto-transition)\n- **When**: Immediately after Management approval\n- **What**:\n  - Review is locked and marked as final\n  - Performance data is available for reports and analytics\n  - Employee receives final performance rating notification\n  - Data feeds into compensation, promotion, and succession planning systems\n- **Deliverables**: Final performance report (PDF export available)\n\n### 6.3 Process Timelines\n\n**Standard Timeline (All Stages):**\n\n- KRA Set: 5 days\n- Self Review: 7 days\n- Manager L1 Check: 3 days\n- Manager L2 Check: 3 days\n- HR PMS Review: 2 days\n- Audit: 2 days\n- Management Review: 2 days\n- **Total: ~24 days (ideal scenario)**\n\n**SLA Compliance Target: 90% of reviews completed within 30 days**\n\n## 7. Key Performance Indicators (KPI) Framework\n\n### 7.1 KPI Principles\n\nAll KPIs must be SMART:\n\n- **Specific**: Clearly defined and unambiguous\n- **Measurable**: Quantifiable with objective criteria\n- **Achievable**: Realistic given resources and constraints\n- **Relevant**: Aligned with role responsibilities and organizational goals\n- **Time-bound**: Tied to specific review periods\n\n### 7.2 KPI Categories (KRAs)\n\n| KRA Category | Description | Typical Weightage |\n|---|---|---|\n| Core Job Responsibilities | Primary duties and deliverables | 40-50% |\n| Quality and Compliance | Adherence to standards and regulations | 15-20% |\n| Innovation and Improvement | Process improvements and new initiatives | 10-15% |\n| Collaboration and Teamwork | Cross-functional cooperation | 10-15% |\n| Learning and Development | Skill enhancement and knowledge sharing | 5-10% |\n| Organizational Values | Alignment with company culture and values | 5-10% |\n\n**Total Weightage: Must equal 100% per employee**\n\n### 7.3 KPI Types\n\n**7.3.1 Numeric KPIs**\n\n- Definition: KPIs measured with numerical values\n- Examples: Sales revenue, production units, customer satisfaction score\n- Scoring: Based on achievement vs. target using R0-R5 thresholds\n\nThreshold Example:\n- R5 (Outstanding): >=120% of target\n- R4 (Exceeds Expectations): 110-119% of target\n- R3 (Meets Expectations): 90-109% of target\n- R2 (Below Expectations): 80-89% of target\n- R1 (Needs Improvement): 70-79% of target\n- R0 (Not Achieved): <70% of target\n\n**7.3.2 Binary KPIs (Yes/No)**\n\n- Definition: KPIs with binary outcomes\n- Examples: Compliance certification obtained, safety audit passed\n- Scoring: Yes = 5 (Outstanding), No = 0 (Not Achieved)\n\nSpecial Case - Daily Binary KPIs: For daily binary KPIs (e.g., \"Daily safety checklist completed\"), monthly score is calculated based on missed days:\n- 0 missed days = 5\n- 1 missed day = 4\n- 2 missed days = 3\n- 3 missed days = 2\n- 4 missed days = 1\n- 5+ missed days = 0\n\n**7.3.3 Tiered KPIs (Custom Options)**\n\n- Definition: KPIs with predefined rating options\n- Examples: Customer feedback (Excellent/Good/Average/Poor)\n- Scoring: Admin-defined ratings per option (0-5 range)\n\n### 7.4 Organization-Level KPIs\n\n- Definition: KPIs that apply to the entire organization or department, not individual employees\n- Scoring Modes: Organization-Wide, Department-Specific, Weighted Contribution\n- Weightage: Organization-level KPIs typically account for 10-20% of individual performance\n\n### 7.5 KPI Templates and Bundles\n\n- KPI Templates: Pre-defined KPIs with standard targets, weightage, and thresholds\n- Template Bundles: Collections of KPI templates grouped by role\n- Customizations require HR approval if they deviate >20% from template weightage\n\n## 8. Rating Scale and Scoring Methodology\n\n### 8.1 Rating Scale (0-5)\n\n| Rating | Level | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 | Outstanding | Consistently exceeds expectations; exceptional performance |\n| 4 | Exceeds Expectations | Frequently exceeds expectations; strong performance |\n| 3 | Meets Expectations | Consistently meets expectations; solid performance |\n| 2 | Below Expectations | Occasionally meets expectations; needs improvement |\n| 1 | Needs Improvement | Rarely meets expectations; significant improvement required |\n| 0 | Not Achieved | Does not meet minimum standards; critical gaps |\n\n### 8.2 Overall Performance Rating Calculation\n\n**Formula:**\n\n```\nOverall Rating = Sum(KPI Rating x KPI Weightage) / Total Effective Weightage\n```\n\n### 8.3 N/A (Not Applicable) KPIs\n\n- Maximum 20% of total weightage can be marked N/A\n- Core job responsibility KPIs cannot be marked N/A without HR approval\n- N/A KPIs are excluded from both numerator and denominator in overall rating calculation\n\n### 8.4 Rating Distribution Guidelines (Forced Ranking - Optional)\n\n| Rating Level | Target Distribution |\n|---|---|\n| Outstanding (5) | 5-10% |\n| Exceeds Expectations (4) | 20-25% |\n| Meets Expectations (3) | 50-60% |\n| Below Expectations (2) | 10-15% |\n| Needs Improvement (1) | 3-5% |\n| Not Achieved (0) | 0-2% |\n\n## 9. Review Cycles and Timelines\n\n### 9.1 Review Frequencies\n\n| Frequency | Description | Typical Use Cases |\n|---|---|---|\n| Daily | Daily performance tracking | Safety compliance, attendance, production targets |\n| Weekly | Weekly performance tracking | Sales calls, project milestones, customer visits |\n| Monthly | Monthly performance reviews | Most common for operational KPIs |\n| Quarterly | Quarterly performance reviews | Strategic initiatives, project-based work |\n| Annual | Annual comprehensive reviews | Overall performance, career development |\n\n### 9.2 Review Periods\n\n- Standard Review Periods: January-December (Annual), Q1-Q4 (Quarterly), Monthly\n- Review periods are locked after all reviews are completed\n- Locked periods cannot be edited (except by System Administrator with audit trail)\n\n### 9.3 Review Calendar\n\n- Day 1 of Period: Review period opens, KPIs assigned\n- Last Day of Period: Review period ends, employee self-review window opens\n- Day 7 after Period End: Employee self-review deadline\n- Day 24 after Period End: All approvals completed (SLA target)\n- Day 30 after Period End: Period locked\n\n## 10. Multi-Level Approval Workflow\n\n### 10.1 Standard Workflow (Full Chain)\n\n```\nEmployee -> RM1 -> RM2 -> HR PMS Team -> Auditor -> Management -> Approved\n```\n\n### 10.2 Simplified Workflow (Shortened Chain)\n\n```\nEmployee -> RM1 -> HR PMS Team -> Approved\n```\n\nApplicable to: Junior-level employees (Grade 1-3), High performers (rating >= 4.5), Roles without RM2\n\n### 10.3 Conditional Workflow (Performance-Based)\n\n- High Performers (Rating >= 4.5): Employee -> RM1 -> Approved (Fast-track)\n- Average Performers (3.0 <= Rating < 4.5): Employee -> RM1 -> HR PMS Team -> Approved\n- Low Performers (Rating < 3.0): Employee -> RM1 -> RM2 -> HR PMS Team -> Auditor -> Management -> PIP Initiation\n\n### 10.4 Department-Specific Workflows\n\nDepartments may define custom workflows (subject to HR approval)\n\n### 10.5 Workflow Configuration\n\nConfigured via Admin -> Approval Chains page. Options: Define approval steps/sequence, set SLA per step, define skip conditions, assign workflows to departments/roles/employees.\n\n## 11. Query and Observation System\n\n### 11.1 Query System\n\n- Formal mechanism for reviewers to request clarification from employees\n- Query Types: Clarification, Discrepancy, Compliance\n- Employee response SLA: 3 business days\n- Reviewer resolution SLA: 2 business days after employee response\n- Queries open >10 days flagged as \"High Priority\"; >20 days flagged as \"Critical\" and escalated to HR\n\n### 11.2 Observation System\n\n- Observation Types: Positive, Concern, Neutral\n- Threaded conversation support\n- Observations are informational only and do not directly impact scores\n\n## 12. Performance Improvement Plans (PIP)\n\n### 12.1 PIP Triggers\n\n- Overall rating <2.5 for two consecutive periods\n- Rating <2.0 in any single period\n- Critical performance gaps identified by management\n- Serious policy violations or misconduct\n\n### 12.2 PIP Process\n\n1. PIP Initiation (RM1 or HR recommends, Management approves)\n2. PIP Development (Collaborative plan with specific gaps, objectives, milestones, duration 30-90 days)\n3. PIP Execution (Ongoing coaching and feedback)\n4. PIP Review (Successful, Partially Successful, Unsuccessful)\n5. Post-PIP Action (Return to normal cycle or further action)\n\n### 12.3 PIP Milestones\n\nEach PIP includes 3-5 milestones with specific deliverables, target dates, expected outcomes, and status tracking.\n\n### 12.4 PIP Rights and Protections\n\n- Right to understand performance gaps\n- Right to receive support and resources\n- Right to appeal PIP decision\n- Right to confidentiality\n\n## 13. Training Needs Identification (TNI)\n\n### 13.1 TNI Purpose\n\nIdentify skill and knowledge gaps requiring training intervention.\n\n### 13.2 TNI Triggers\n\n- Rating <3.0 on specific KPIs\n- Manager or employee identifies skill gaps\n- New technologies or processes require upskilling\n- Career development plans require new competencies\n\n### 13.3 TNI Process\n\n1. Gap Identification (auto-detect KPIs with ratings <3.0)\n2. Training Recommendation (formal, on-the-job, self-directed)\n3. Training Approval (HR reviews and approves)\n4. Training Completion\n5. Follow-Up (monitor performance in subsequent periods)\n\n### 13.4 TNI Priority Levels\n\n| Priority | Description | Action Timeline |\n|---|---|---|\n| Critical | Immediate impact on job performance or safety | Within 30 days |\n| High | Significant impact on performance | Within 60 days |\n| Medium | Moderate impact, development opportunity | Within 90 days |\n| Low | Nice-to-have, long-term development | Within 180 days |\n\n## 14. Appeals and Grievance Procedures\n\n### 14.1 Grounds for Appeal\n\n- Procedural Error\n- Bias or Discrimination\n- Factual Inaccuracy\n- Inconsistent Application\n- New Evidence\n\n### 14.2 Appeal Process\n\n1. Informal Resolution (discuss with RM1)\n2. Formal Appeal Submission (written to HR within 10 business days)\n3. Appeal Review (HR investigation)\n4. Appeal Decision (HR or Management)\n5. Outcome Communication\n\n### 14.3 Appeal Timelines\n\n- Appeal submission: 10 business days from final rating\n- HR investigation: 10 business days\n- Management review (if escalated): 15 business days\n- Total maximum: 25 business days\n\n### 14.4 Protection Against Retaliation\n\nEmployees who raise appeals or grievances in good faith are protected from retaliation.\n\n## 15. Data Privacy and Security\n\n### 15.1 Data Privacy Principles\n\n- Confidentiality, Data Minimization, Purpose Limitation, Accuracy, Retention\n\n### 15.2 Data Access Controls\n\n| Role | Access Level |\n|---|---|\n| Employee | Own performance data only |\n| RM1 | Direct reports'' performance data |\n| RM2 | Skip-level reports'' performance data |\n| HR PMS Team | All performance data (for validation and reporting) |\n| Auditor | All performance data (for audit purposes) |\n| Management | Performance data for designated employee levels |\n| System Administrator | Technical access (with audit logging) |\n\n### 15.3 Data Security Measures\n\n- Encryption at rest and in transit (TLS/SSL)\n- Row-Level Security (RLS) database policies\n- Audit logging for all data access and modifications\n- Daily automated backups with 30-day retention\n\n### 15.4 Employee Data Rights\n\n- Access, Correction, Explanation, Export (PDF/Excel), Deletion (subject to legal retention)\n\n### 15.5 Data Retention\n\n- Active Performance Data: Retained while employee is active\n- Historical Data: 7 years after employee separation\n- Audit Logs: 10 years\n- Backup Data: 30 days (rolling)\n\n## 16. Compliance and Legal Requirements\n\n### 16.1 Non-Discrimination and Equal Opportunity\n\nPerformance evaluations conducted without regard to race, color, ethnicity, gender, age, disability, religion, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n### 16.2 Reasonable Accommodations\n\nEmployees with disabilities entitled to reasonable accommodations including modified KPIs, extended timelines, alternative documentation formats, and assistive technology support.\n\n### 16.3 Compliance Monitoring\n\n- Quarterly internal compliance audits\n- Annual comprehensive PMS audit\n- Cooperation with external regulatory audits\n\n## 17. Policy Governance and Amendments\n\n### 17.1 Policy Ownership\n\n- Policy Owner: CHRO\n- Policy Custodian: HR PMS Team\n- Policy Approver: Board of Directors / Management Committee\n\n### 17.2 Policy Review and Updates\n\n- Review Frequency: Annual (or as needed)\n- Major Amendments: Require Management Committee approval with minimum 30 days notice\n- Minor Amendments: Approved by CHRO\n\n### 17.3 Policy Violations\n\n- Falsification of performance data\n- Unauthorized access to performance records\n- Retaliation against employees for appeals\n- Discrimination or bias in evaluations\n- Failure to complete reviews within SLA (repeated violations)\n\nConsequences: Investigation by HR, disciplinary action per organization''s disciplinary policy\n\n## 18. Appendices\n\n### Appendix A: PMS Process Flowchart\n\n```\nSTART\n  |\n  v\n1. KRA Set       <- RM1 assigns KPIs to Employee\n  |\n  v\n2. Self Review   <- Employee submits self-assessment\n  |\n  v\n3. Manager L1    <- RM1 reviews and approves\n   Check\n  |\n  v\n4. Manager L2    <- RM2 validates (if applicable)\n   Check\n  |\n  v\n5. HR PMS Review <- HR validates compliance\n  |\n  v\n6. Audit         <- Auditor checks (if applicable)\n  |\n  v\n7. Management    <- Management final approval\n   Review\n  |\n  v\n8. APPROVED      <- Review completed and locked\n  |\n  v\nEND\n```\n\n### Appendix B: Rating Scale Reference Card\n\n| Rating | Level | % of Target | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | Outstanding | >=120% | Exceptional, top 10% |\n| 4 | Exceeds Expectations | 110-119% | Strong, top 11-30% |\n| 3 | Meets Expectations | 90-109% | Solid, middle 40% |\n| 2 | Below Expectations | 80-89% | Needs improvement |\n| 1 | Needs Improvement | 70-79% | Significant gaps |\n| 0 | Not Achieved | <70% | Critical gaps |\n\n### Appendix C: Sample KPI Template (Sales Executive)\n\n| KRA | KPI | Target | Weightage | UOM |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sales Performance | Monthly Revenue | $50,000 | 40% | USD |\n| Customer Acquisition | New Customers | 10 | 20% | Nos |\n| Customer Retention | Retention Rate | 90% | 15% | % |\n| Quality | Customer Satisfaction | 4.5/5 | 15% | Score |\n| Compliance | CRM Data Entry | Yes | 10% | Binary |\n\n### Appendix D: Contact Information\n\n- HR PMS Team: pms@company.com\n- System Support: pms-support@company.com\n\n---\n\n*This policy is effective from the Effective Date and supersedes all previous performance management policies. All employees are required to read, understand, and comply with this policy.*',
